      feat: use latest upsteam php
      
      This requires several changes:
      - Updates the core submodule to use a more recent version which supports
        tree-sitter 0.26.3. This is needed since latest upstream php uses
        features (namely `reserved`) which are only avaliable in 0.25.0 or
        later.
      - Updates languages/language-variants-$VERSION files to reflect this.
      - Upstream has split the grammar into both `php` and `php-only` (the
        former allows markup tags) so we have to make some updates here. We
        already had a configuration like this for typescript and tsx, so much
        of this is just copied from what we do for those (e.g., the
        `semgrep-grammars/src/semgrep-php/prep` file is essentially just a
        port of the same for typescript)
